/-!
# The place of a function field at a point of codimension one with normal stalk

Route (a) of §3.1 of `Submission/Work/FFResidual/NOTES.md`: a **point of codimension one whose
local ring is normal** produces a place of the function field of an integral locally Noetherian
scheme over its constants — hence `Work.FFResidual.HasFunctionFieldPlace` for such a scheme.

Concretely, for `X` an integral locally Noetherian scheme and `z : X` a point with
`Order.coheight z = 1`, the stalk `𝒪_{X,z}`

* is a Noetherian local domain (scheme theory),
* has Krull dimension one (`AnalysisGeometry.ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_coheight`), so that
  `Ring.KrullDimLE 1 𝒪_{X,z}` (`AlgebraicGeometry.krullDimLE_of_coheight_le`), and
* has fraction field `X.functionField` (`AlgebraicGeometry.IsFractionRing (X.presheaf.stalk z)
  X.functionField`),

and a one-dimensional Noetherian local domain which is integrally closed — a *normal* local ring —
is a **discrete valuation ring** (a classical theorem of commutative algebra, reduced here to
Mathlib's `IsDiscreteValuationRing.TFAE`).  Its maximal ideal is generated by any irreducible
element (`IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible`), which is the uniformizer of the place.

This file supplies the geometric input of the function-field classes (b), (c), (d) of
Lin–Shinder, *Motivic invariants of birational maps*, Annals of Math. **199** (1), 2024,
Theorem 1.2 (1): `HasFunctionFieldPlace 𝔽 X.functionField` once one knows that the constants act
on the stalk and on the function field compatibly (`IsScalarTower 𝔽 𝒪_{X,z} X.functionField`).

## Main results

* `Work.FFResidual.Geometry.isDiscreteValuationRing_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_krullDimLE_one_aux` —
  a one-dimensional Noetherian integrally closed local domain is a discrete valuation ring.
* `Work.FFResidual.Geometry.hasFunctionFieldPlace_of_coheight_one_stalk` — the place of
  `X.functionField` over `𝔽` at a codimension-one point with integrally closed stalk.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.style.haveILetI false

namespace Work.FFResidual.Geometry

/-- **A one-dimensional Noetherian normal local domain is a discrete valuation ring.**

This is the commutative-algebra core of the construction of the place: `R` is a Noetherian local
domain of Krull dimension `≤ 1` which is integrally closed in its fraction field (i.e. normal) and
not a field; then `R` is a discrete valuation ring.

The proof goes through Mathlib's `IsDiscreteValuationRing.TFAE`: the hypotheses say exactly that
`R` is Dedekind (Noetherian, of dimension `≤ 1`, integrally closed), and a *local* Dedekind domain
which is not a field is a discrete valuation ring.

(Stated as a lemma about an abstract commutative ring so that it is reusable; it is the statement
of `Submission/Work/FFResidual/Geometry/isDiscreteValuationRing_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_krullDimLE_one`,
which is proved here under a name of its own so that this file stays self-contained.) -/
theorem isDiscreteValuationRing_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_krullDimLE_one_aux
    (R : Type) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] (hnf : ¬ IsField R) :
    IsDiscreteValuationRing R := by
  -- `R` is a Dedekind domain: it is Noetherian, of dimension `≤ 1`, and integrally closed.
  haveI : IsDedekindDomain R :=
    { ‹IsIntegrallyClosed R› with
        maximalOfPrime := fun {p} hp hpp =>
          Ring.krullDimLE_one_iff_of_noZeroDivisors.mp ‹Ring.KrullDimLE 1 R› p hp hpp }
  -- A local Dedekind domain is a PID, and a local PID which is not a field is a DVR.
  exact { not_a_field' := IsLocalRing.isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq.not.mp hnf }

-- Please declare this in namespace `Work.FFResidual.Geometry`.
/-- **The place of the function field `X.functionField` over `𝔽` at a codimension-one point `z`
whose local ring is normal.**

For `X` an integral locally Noetherian scheme, `z : X` a point of coheight one with integrally
closed stalk, and compatible algebra structures `𝔽 → 𝒪_{X,z} → X.functionField`, the local ring
`𝒪_{X,z}` is a discrete valuation ring with fraction field `X.functionField`; it is therefore the
valuation ring of a place of `X.functionField` over `𝔽`, and a uniformizer of that place is any
irreducible element of `𝒪_{X,z}`. -/
theorem hasFunctionFieldPlace_of_coheight_one_stalk
    {𝔽 : Type} [Field 𝔽] {X : AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme}
    [AlgebraicGeometry.IsIntegral X] [AlgebraicGeometry.IsLocallyNoetherian X] {z : X}
    [Algebra 𝔽 X.functionField] [Algebra 𝔽 (X.presheaf.stalk z)]
    [IsScalarTower 𝔽 (X.presheaf.stalk z) X.functionField]
    (hz : Order.coheight z = 1) (hint : IsIntegrallyClosed (X.presheaf.stalk z)) :
    Work.FFResidual.HasFunctionFieldPlace 𝔽 X.functionField := by
  -- The stalk at a point of coheight one has Krull dimension `≤ 1`.
  haveI hKLE : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 (X.presheaf.stalk z) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.krullDimLE_of_coheight_le hz.le
  -- It is not a field: a field has Krull dimension zero, while the dimension of the stalk is the
  -- coheight of the point, which is one.
  have hnf : ¬ IsField (X.presheaf.stalk z) := by
    intro hfield
    have h0 : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk z) = 0 := ringKrullDim_eq_zero_of_isField hfield
    have h1 : ringKrullDim (X.presheaf.stalk z) = Order.coheight z :=
      AlgebraicGeometry.ringKrullDim_stalk_eq_coheight z
    rw [h1, hz] at h0
    exact one_ne_zero h0
  -- So the stalk is a discrete valuation ring, with fraction field the function field.
  haveI hDVR : IsDiscreteValuationRing (X.presheaf.stalk z) :=
    isDiscreteValuationRing_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_krullDimLE_one_aux _ hnf
  -- Any irreducible element generates the maximal ideal, hence is a uniformizer.
  obtain ⟨π, hπ⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible (X.presheaf.stalk z)
  exact ⟨{ R := X.presheaf.stalk z, π := π, isUniformizer := hπ.maximalIdeal_eq }⟩

end Work.FFResidual.Geometry
